{"kind":"event","event_id":7059,"event_uid":"01M2NP6TBA5N68HE3PYGWJN1HD","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":303,"issue_uid":"01M2NP3KB5B3D2V4QMTSR7X49C","issue_short_id":"x49c","actor":"impl:1@run-165","hlc_physical_ms":1789581814122,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"2295c139761fa7985f35e7e35d633c7c8058ac8ec635bdf283c85d97d7f49f0c","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NP6TB9M2DDFK4RGZ7RW8TR","author":"impl:1@run-165","body":"Task 1 approach: two module-level pure helpers in fleet/run-engine.mjs beside addedExportsOf — nulOffsetOf(buf) (Buffer.indexOf(0), -1 when absent) and async nulIntroducedBy({paths, declared, readNow, readBase}) returning {path, offset} rows in the given order. Then a nulReds() closure in runTaskInner mirroring exportCollisions() exactly: called at the end of prePass after the collision scan, over patchPaths(impl.patch), declared = task.files, readNow = fs.readFileSync in cloneDir, readBase = exec('git', ['show', baseShaForTask + ':' + p], {cwd: cloneDir}) with a non-zero exit read as null. Each row pushes one red {line, stdout:''} and one driver:finding at round 0. CONTRACT.md gets the NUL sentence appended to the pre-review collision paragraph.","created_at":"2026-09-16T18:03:34.121402255Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T18:03:34.122Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7060,"event_uid":"01M2NP8NX75NX5GYYWPDBVS6QG","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":303,"issue_uid":"01M2NP3KB5B3D2V4QMTSR7X49C","issue_short_id":"x49c","actor":"exam:1@run-165","hlc_physical_ms":1789581875111,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"c09eeb893e69d5fdd0c585a95054923f007d097cadf30fb1ac9464eba43b3d64","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NP8NX62FC3XBW6T9EJCXZQ","author":"exam:1@run-165","body":"examiner, round 1: writing `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_nul_guard.mjs` whole at its guarded path, on the shape of the sibling collision sim (rig + canned stub keyed on `opts.label`, `findingsAtRoundZero`). Leg (a) drives `nulOffsetOf`/`nulIntroducedBy` directly with canned async readers over the seven paths; legs (b)(c)(d) are real one-task runs whose implementer writes the raw 0x00 / the two-character escape / plain text / a modified base-binary / a Files-named PNG; (f)(g)(h) are the CONTRACT.md range, the four engine files read as bytes, and this file's own import lines. Leg (e) names the sibling collision sim, which a sim may not spawn (`test_sims_are_hermetic.mjs` M4) — what stands for it here is M4's own sentence asserted directly: one run with a `Run:` and a `Check:` whose `driver:proof-run`/`driver:check-run`/`driver:exam-run` rows are exactly BASE's. Validating the rig mechanics (binary capture, fold of a binary deliverable) in a scratch tree before writing the file.","created_at":"2026-09-16T18:04:35.110050042Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T18:04:35.111Z"}
